{
  "corpus_id": "soveraeign-automation-health-cases/v1",
  "note": "Positive and defeating cases for contracts/automation-health.json. Every rule in that table carries at least one case that proves it fires and one that proves it stays quiet when it should, because a rule with only a firing case proves nothing about what it lets past. Runs are listed oldest first. Times are inputs to the judge, not measurements of anything, and no case reads .claude/schedules/ or the ledger - the corpus states facts so the rules can be defeated without a run ever having happened.",
  "run_shape": "Each run states what the ledger holds: attempted_at with the ATTEMPTED event outcome, then reported_at with the REPORTED event outcome, or nulls where no REPORTED event exists, plus the exit code and the output addresses that event recorded. expect_status names the run status contracts/automation-health.json run_status derives from that pair, so the derivation is defeated here too and not only the rules above it. A schedule block also carries declaration_defect: what scripts/sovschedule/declaration.py said when it refused the file, or null when it accepted it.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "H-001-a-declaration-pointing-at-nothing-refuses-even-switched-off",
      "schedule": {
        "name": "ghost",
        "enabled": false,
        "target_exists": false,
        "cron": "0 2 * * *",
        "timeout_seconds": 3600,
        "declaration_defect": "ghost.json: workflow 'sov-ghost' not found under .claude/"
      },
      "now": "2026-08-27T04:00:00Z",
      "runs": [],
      "expect_status": [],
      "expect_findings": [
        "TARGET_MISSING"
      ],
      "expect_reading": "UNHEALTHY",
      "proves": "TARGET_MISSING fires. A dead target is broken whether or not the schedule is on: enabling it would otherwise be the moment anyone found out, and this is the one rule a machine with no run history can still evaluate. It is also the near miss for DECLARATION_REFUSED - the loader refuses this file too, and that rule stands down so one defect is not reported twice, with the loader's text carried on this finding instead so nothing is lost."
    },
    {
      "case_id": "H-002-seven-declared-none-enabled-nothing-ever-run-is-not-healthy",
      "schedule": {
        "name": "nightly-qa",
        "enabled": false,
        "target_exists": true,
        "cron": "0 2 * * *",
        "timeout_seconds": 3600,
        "declaration_defect": null
      },
      "now": "2026-08-27T04:00:00Z",
      "runs": [],
      "expect_status": [],
      "expect_findings": [],
      "expect_reading": "UNOBSERVED",
      "proves": "TARGET_MISSING stays quiet against a target that exists, and the reading is UNOBSERVED rather than HEALTHY. This is the state of all seven schedules on 2026-08-27 and it is the case the whole table exists for: an empty record set must not report green."
    },
    {
      "case_id": "H-019-a-declaration-that-will-not-load-is-not-a-schedule",
      "schedule": {
        "name": "epic-walk",
        "enabled": false,
        "target_exists": true,
        "cron": "0 7 * *",
        "timeout_seconds": 3600,
        "declaration_defect": "epic-walk.json: cron '0 7 * *': needs five fields, got 4"
      },
      "now": "2026-08-27T04:00:00Z",
      "runs": [],
      "expect_status": [],
      "expect_findings": [
        "DECLARATION_REFUSED"
      ],
      "expect_reading": "UNHEALTHY",
      "proves": "DECLARATION_REFUSED fires and refuses. The target is there, so TARGET_MISSING is quiet and this rule carries the defect. It also proves the surface survives a file the loader will not take: every other verb in scripts/sov_schedule.py raises on the first such file and shows nothing at all, which on a seeing surface would hide the six schedules that are fine behind the one that is not. OVERDUE stays quiet rather than raising on the same unparseable expression."
    },
